506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 297 0 R
/E (There are three primary types of mobile wallet apps: universal proximity wallets, branded store proximity wallets, and P2P apps. Universal proximity mobile wallets, such as Apple Pay, Google Pay, and Samsung Pay, that can be used at a variety of mer- chants for point-of-sale transactions if the merchant supports that service \(e.g., has an Apple merchant app and can accept such payments\), are the most-well known and common type. Branded store proximity mobile wallets are mobile apps that can be used only at a single merchant. For instance, Walmart, Tesco, and Starbucks all have very successful mobile wallet apps. P2P mobile payment apps, such as Venmo and Square Cash, are used for payments among individuals who have the same app. )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [1]
>>
