<<
/Title (A flaw in the OpenSSL encryption system, used by millions of websites, known as the Heartbleed bug, was discovered . The vulnerability allowed hackers to decrypt an SSL session and discover user names, passwords, and other user data, by using OpenSSL in combination with a communications protocol called the RFC6520 heartbeat that helps a remote user remain in touch after connecting with a website server.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1764 0 R
